            <abstract>
                <gco:CharacterString>     Planned major transit stops included in the 2020 Metropolitan Transportation Plan/Sustainable Communities Strategy (MTP/SCS) by the horizon year of the plan (2040). These areas are subject to change with each MTP/SCS adoption. For reference, a major transit stop is as defined in Public Resources Code Section 21064.3 below, except that, for the purposes of this shapefile, it only includes major transit stops that are planned in the adopted MTP/SCS by the horizon year of the plan (2040): A major transit stop is defined as a site containing a site containing any of the following: An existing rail or bus rapid transit station.A ferry terminal served by either a bus or rail transit service. The intersection of two or more major bus routes with a frequency of service interval of 20 minutes or less during the morning and afternoon peak commute periods.</gco:CharacterString>
            </abstract>
            <purpose>
                <gco:CharacterString>Planned major transit stops included in the 2020 Metropolitan Transportation Plan/Sustainable Communities Strategy (MTP/SCS) by the horizon year of the plan (2040).
</gco:CharacterString>
